6B. PYTHON ATOMS, MONEY AND TIME
=======================================================================
KEEP FROM THE CANDIDATES - never drop them from the final table: source_kind on every FACTS row, the steps
(step1, step2 ...), rule, when and result of every python atom, amount / unit on the OR row. A candidate that wrote
a calculated value as a FACTS row (WORKED_OUT, derivation): move that formula into a step of its atom. If the candidates differ,
keep the one that follows the rules below; if both missed a calculation the law states, add it.
PYTHON ATOMS, MONEY AND TIME - FACTS ARE RAW INPUTS, THE CALCULATION IS INSIDE THE ATOM
A python atom is decided by Python ALONE at validation time: no reading, no judgement, the same answer every
time. So it must carry everything Python needs: its raw input facts and every calculation step. Money and time
laws (tax, interest, late fee, penalty, refund, credit share, threshold, due date, time limit) are almost always
python - they are the most valuable checks, because they give the issue in rupees.

1. WHAT IS PYTHON AND WHAT IS NOT
   python : printed values and dates compared (invoice value > 50000), thresholds (turnover > 2000000), date
            limits (credit claimed by the deadline), days of delay, register / table lookups (GSTIN status, HSN ->
            rate, due date of a return), two documents matched (ITC in books vs GSTR-2B), same / different state,
            sums, and every money formula (tax, interest, fee, penalty, cap, rounding).
   never  : what must be UNDERSTOOD from text or the transaction - form of supply (sale / rental / barter),
            goods or services, course or furtherance of business, related person, purpose of use, nature of an
            activity. Those facts are source_kind READ and their atoms are light / heavy.

2. A FACT IS A RAW INPUT - NEVER A CALCULATED VALUE
   Every FACTS row is a value that comes from outside and can be mapped to a field of a document or a register.
   source_kind on EVERY TXN FACTS row (a registry fact too):
     DOCUMENT  printed on a document that is checked (invoice date, taxable value, filing date of a return)
     LOOKUP    taken from a register, master or table by a key (GSTIN status, due date of a return for its tax
               period, rate of an HSN, a rate / limit / fee fixed by a notification or by the law, the date of
               the check). Its evidence names the source (evidence: [Notification 13/2017-CT], [section 47(1)]).
     READ      an AI must read free text to decide it (step 1, never python)
     ASK       only a person can answer
   NEVER write a FACTS row for something calculated (days late, failure end date, fee, interest, cap, excess
   credit): write it as a STEP of the atom (step 3). A python atom uses only DOCUMENT and LOOKUP facts.

3. THE ATOM CARRIES ITS CALCULATION - step1, step2 ... IN ORDER
   On the A row:  facts: [every raw fact the steps use];
                  step1: "<name> = <formula>"; step2: "<name> = <formula>"; ...
                  rule: "<a step or a fact compared with a VALUE>"
   - A step name is lower case words joined by _ (failure_end, days_late, late_fee). It is NOT a fact and is never
     a FACTS row. Python ids (F_..., A_...) stay as you write them; only facts are mapped to fields.
   - A step may use: the atom's facts, numbers, earlier steps of the same atom, and <WHEN_ATOM>.<step> - a step of
     the atom named in `when`.
   - Formula grammar (Python checks it and runs it - nothing else is allowed):
       F_ facts, step names, numbers (100, 0.25), quoted codes ('LATE'), TRUE / FALSE
       + - * / ( )     = != > >= < <=     AND OR NOT
       MIN(a, b, ...)  MAX(a, b, ...)  ROUND(x)  ROUND(x, 2)  ABS(x)  IF(condition, then, else)
       DAYS_BETWEEN(from, to)  MONTHS_BETWEEN(from, to)  ADD_DAYS(d, n)  ADD_MONTHS(d, n)  END_OF_MONTH(d)
       DATE(year, month, day)  YEAR(d)  MONTH(d)  DAY(d)
   - The rule is a comparison: rule: "days_late > 0". Without steps the rule compares a fact with a value
     (rule: "F_PRS = 'REGISTERED'").
   - A number written in THIS law's text may be in a step AND stays in the atom statement in the law's words
     ("one hundred rupees"). A number the government notifies or changes (a rate, a due date, a reduced fee) is a
     LOOKUP fact - never invent its value.
   - "for every day during which such failure continues": the days run from the due date to the day the return is
     furnished, or to the date of the check when it is not furnished yet - write that with IF.

4. AN AMOUNT ATOM CARRIES THE MONEY
   The consequence in money ("shall pay a late fee of ...", "shall pay interest at ...") is its own atom:
     role: CONSEQUENCE; order: LOW; handler: python; when: <the condition atom that must be TRUE first>;
     facts: [...]; step1 ...; rule: "<amount step> > 0"; result: <the step that is the amount>
   It needs no LE or group (it hangs on its `when` atom).
   OR row of the outcome: amount: <AMOUNT_ATOM>.<result step>; unit: INR - the rupee impact of the law.

